WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.569
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Kenan Thompson.

00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:04.771
This is really cool,
speaking about

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:06.672
how long you've been
on the show.

00:00:06.672 --> 00:00:09.675
Aubrey Plaza hosting this week,
the fantastic Aubrey Plaza,

00:00:09.675 --> 00:00:11.878
was, in 2004,
when we were both there,

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:12.912
an intern in the set department.

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:14.080
-Is that not crazy?

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.482
-What a trip.
Now the interns are coming back.

00:00:16.482 --> 00:00:17.483
That's how long
you've been there.

00:00:17.483 --> 00:00:18.684
-Yeah, I know.

00:00:18.684 --> 00:00:20.420
So I'm going to start hurting
at some point.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:22.688
-Yeah. I will say --
and I think this reflects

00:00:22.688 --> 00:00:25.324
very well on you --
this is a real reminder --

00:00:25.324 --> 00:00:26.693
be nice to the interns,

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:28.427
which I'm sure
you always have been.

00:00:28.427 --> 00:00:29.529
-1,000%.

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:30.863
Like, all this week,
I've been like,

00:00:30.863 --> 00:00:34.867
"I feel like I was nice to her,
but do I know for sure?"

00:00:34.867 --> 00:00:38.271
-We all do have bad days,
but it's a real mistake

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:42.375
to take it out on the interns,
because just based on, you know,

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:43.942
life expectancy,
they're going to be around

00:00:43.942 --> 00:00:46.679
after we're long gone.

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:47.847
We were talking about --
You know,

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:49.181
I have authors
on the show a lot.

00:00:49.181 --> 00:00:50.483
-Yes, you do.

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:54.020
-And you were lamenting the fact
that you've never been on

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:56.422
to talk about your book,
because I, of course,

00:00:56.422 --> 00:00:58.691
did not know --
or certainly assumed that

00:00:58.691 --> 00:00:59.725
you hadn't written a book,
but you actually have been

00:00:59.725 --> 00:01:01.194
writing books.

00:01:01.194 --> 00:01:06.599
-Yes, I've been dabbling in the
world of authoring, if you will.

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:09.769
And, yeah, I'm very excited to

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:11.504
present some of my work
here tonight.

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:13.739
-And you write under a pen name.

00:01:13.739 --> 00:01:15.074
-I do. A full pen name.
-Okay.

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:17.643
Would you like to leave
and have me introduce you

00:01:17.643 --> 00:01:18.778
as your pen name?

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:20.145
-Oh, that's fun.
Yeah, can we do that?

00:01:20.145 --> 00:01:21.147
-Yeah.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:22.381
-Okay, go ahead.
-Okay, I'm going.

00:01:22.381 --> 00:01:24.350
Okay, I'll be right back.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:30.289 --> 00:01:31.891
-This is really exciting,
everybody.

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:36.229
Our next guest is
a science-fiction writer

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:39.599
with the third
in his "Quark" series.

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:43.202
Please welcome the author of
"Quinsley's Nebula,"

00:01:43.202 --> 00:01:44.971
Pernice LaFonk.

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:47.006
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:08.495
Oh, my God.

00:02:08.495 --> 00:02:11.030
Mr. LaFonk, what an honor
to have you here.

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:16.436
-Sethly, it is
an honor and a privilege

00:02:16.436 --> 00:02:19.072
to be graced with your presence,
as well, my friend.

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:22.542
-Now, you are
a science-fiction writer.

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:24.544
Where do you get
your wonderful ideas about

00:02:24.544 --> 00:02:26.645
space and these
fantastic characters?

00:02:26.645 --> 00:02:29.248
-Oh, the cosmos provides.

00:02:29.248 --> 00:02:31.283
The cosmos
most definitely provides.

00:02:31.283 --> 00:02:34.053
And I would just love to
read a bit of my...

00:02:34.053 --> 00:02:35.388
-Do you want to read a passage?
-...my work.

00:02:35.388 --> 00:02:37.256
-Well, here we go.
This is so exciting.

00:02:37.256 --> 00:02:38.757
And I've read all the books
in the "Quark" series,

00:02:38.757 --> 00:02:39.926
so this is very exciting.

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:43.729
-And you respect mine.
Thank you very much.

00:02:43.729 --> 00:02:45.431
Wonderful.

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:47.199
[ Clears throat ]

00:02:47.199 --> 00:02:53.339
The name of the book is
"Quinsley's Nebula."

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:57.010
Here is a passage from
Chapter 13, "Beta 4."

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:01.080
-Your chapters always have
the most wonderful titles.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:04.017
-Yes. Big fan of "Star Wars."

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:08.721
"There is thunder
on the planet Persephone 9."

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:11.657
Mm.

00:03:11.657 --> 00:03:14.760
"But it makes not the cracking
sound it does on Earth.

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:18.163
Rather,
it makes a different noise

00:03:18.163 --> 00:03:22.001
every...single...time.

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:26.372
No sound of thunder ever repeats
on this barren planet,

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:28.975
a fact that
Captain Grax Pendlesmith

00:03:28.975 --> 00:03:33.345
was unaware of as he steered
his ship to an uneasy landing

00:03:33.345 --> 00:03:35.314
amidst the swirling storm.

00:03:35.314 --> 00:03:37.516
'Kerflank!'

00:03:37.516 --> 00:03:41.787
went the thunder as
his trusty ship, the Pegaseuss,

00:03:41.787 --> 00:03:43.222
lurched to the right.

00:03:43.222 --> 00:03:47.393
'Ba-klamp!' went the next,

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:49.862
followed by a
'Paloma,' 'Shalamar,'

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:52.131
and, finally, 'Futhermucker.'"

00:03:52.131 --> 00:03:54.400
Thank you. Thank you very much.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.368
[ Cheers and applause ]
Good times.

00:03:56.368 --> 00:03:58.403
-So wonderful.

00:03:58.403 --> 00:03:59.672
-Thank you very much.

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:03.276
-And, now, you are doing
a book signing at

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:05.211
Barnes &amp; Noble tonight?

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:06.512
-Not tonight.

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:07.913
Very early in the morning,

00:04:07.913 --> 00:04:10.649
if you wouldn't mind
showing up at 5:00 a.m.

00:04:10.649 --> 00:04:12.551
I will be there promptly
at 5:07.

00:04:12.551 --> 00:04:14.153
-Now, I don't even think
Barnes &amp; Noble

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:15.321
is open that early.

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:16.356
Are you doing it outside
the Barnes &amp; Noble?

00:04:16.356 --> 00:04:20.526
-If it's ideal, on the sidewalk.

00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:22.995
-So you're doing
a book signing on the sidewalk

00:04:22.995 --> 00:04:24.096
outside of Barnes &amp; Noble.

00:04:24.096 --> 00:04:26.799
-Yes. I'm very brave.
Very brave.

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:28.234
And I'm looking forward to it.

00:04:28.234 --> 00:04:32.705
Also, I will be introducing
my following, follow-up book,

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:35.074
"Amazon Boobies on the Moon."

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:37.110
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.312 --> 00:04:42.148
So look out for that series.
-Where did you get that idea?

00:04:42.148 --> 00:04:43.483
-I think in the shower.

00:04:43.483 --> 00:04:47.186
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:48.287
-Now, what do you smoke?

00:04:48.287 --> 00:04:49.588
Could I just ask
real quick, Pernice,

00:04:49.588 --> 00:04:50.656
what do you usually smoke?

00:04:50.656 --> 00:04:53.492
-I think you know.

00:04:53.492 --> 00:04:55.761
I think you know.

00:04:55.761 --> 00:04:57.095
We don't want to --
-And this is very exciting.

00:04:57.095 --> 00:05:01.333
I know that Netflix
is adapting this into a series,

00:05:01.333 --> 00:05:05.371
and there is some really
exciting casting news you have.

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:06.605
-Is that happening?

00:05:06.605 --> 00:05:08.107
Oh.

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:10.610
I wasn't aware of that.

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:14.113
I'm very excited
to hear their plans.

00:05:14.113 --> 00:05:16.616
-Do you even
have a Netflix account?

00:05:16.616 --> 00:05:21.287
-And could you explain,
what is this Netflix, exactly?

00:05:21.287 --> 00:05:22.688
This is fun.

00:05:22.688 --> 00:05:25.857
-Pernice LaFonk, you, of course,
are also Kenan Thompson.

00:05:25.857 --> 00:05:27.225
You are a dear friend.

00:05:27.225 --> 00:05:30.262
Give it up one more time...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:30.262 --> 00:05:31.931
for Kenan, everybody.

00:05:31.931 --> 00:05:35.101
"SNL" returns and this week with

00:05:35.101 --> 00:05:37.770
host Aubrey Plaza
and musical guest Sam Smith.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:41.074
We'll be right back with
Jinkx Monsoon.

